WEBVTT

00:03.460 --> 00:04.750
Mr. Bernard!

00:07.420 --> 00:08.790
MR. BERNARD!

00:09.130 --> 00:10.380
Where's Teach?!

00:10.380 --> 00:11.670
We need to get him here, fast!

00:12.130 --> 00:14.710
The boss won't be coming for us.

00:15.210 --> 00:19.670
This is a battle we have to win on our own.

00:23.710 --> 00:24.920
There he is!

00:26.960 --> 00:28.170
Is he okay?

00:28.170 --> 00:29.380
He's breathing.

00:29.380 --> 00:30.710
He's going to make it.

00:30.710 --> 00:33.710
You just said that Klaus wasn't here.

00:33.710 --> 00:34.960
What did you mean?

00:35.250 --> 00:36.580
Exactly what I said.

00:36.920 --> 00:38.460
So, that's what's up.

00:38.540 --> 00:40.670
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:40.670 --> 00:43.210
Teach came and visited us all the time.

00:43.380 --> 00:45.540
That was Grete in disguise.

00:46.540 --> 00:50.500
All those times we saw Teach, it was always just Grete.

00:51.250 --> 00:53.750
So wait, when we ran into him that one time...

00:54.580 --> 00:56.790
And that meeting I had...

00:57.250 --> 00:58.250
That's right.

00:58.250 --> 01:00.830
You didn't just disguise yourself
as the assassin with the birthmark,

01:00.830 --> 01:03.210
but as Teach, too?

01:03.460 --> 01:06.960
I memorized the way the boss breathes,
the way he blinks,

01:06.960 --> 01:10.210
and the position of every hair on his head.

01:10.830 --> 01:12.960
Damn, you're really somethin' else!

01:12.960 --> 01:14.790
I do happen to be plenty good at crossdressing.

01:14.790 --> 01:17.130
Are you still mad about that?

01:18.000 --> 01:22.500
In any case, the boss is at
a different mission site right now.

01:22.500 --> 01:23.880
What mission?

01:23.880 --> 01:25.540
The assassin hunt.

01:25.710 --> 01:28.380
Corpse was never the one hiding in the mansion.

01:28.380 --> 01:31.460
It was his associate, Olivia.

01:32.170 --> 01:37.330
Teach wants us to capture Olivia
while he goes and fights Corpse.

01:37.330 --> 01:38.960
That about sum it up?

01:39.170 --> 01:40.170
It does.

01:40.170 --> 01:43.170
So, Teach is all on his own again?

01:43.330 --> 01:45.630
That whole thing about picking four people was a lie?

01:45.630 --> 01:46.880
That was no lie.

01:47.580 --> 01:49.790
He picked four people just fine.

01:50.130 --> 01:52.960
Thea, Monika, Annette, Erna:

01:52.960 --> 01:56.670
Those were the four he took with him to go kill Corpse.

01:58.710 --> 02:00.580
We're the team members who got left out.

02:01.210 --> 02:02.460
We didn't make the cut.

02:03.580 --> 02:04.880
Magnificent.

02:06.960 --> 02:08.170
It's me.

02:08.960 --> 02:11.880
I left Grete with a message to pass along to you.

02:12.420 --> 02:14.540
I'm sorry for tricking you.

02:15.290 --> 02:20.380
Making the enemy spy lurking in the mansion
think that I was close at hand

02:20.380 --> 02:22.710
was the best way I had of protecting you.

02:23.040 --> 02:25.130
With any luck, it should have held them in check.

02:27.750 --> 02:31.170
Also, there was a very specific reason

02:28.750 --> 02:31.880
Embrace the toll of pain

02:31.170 --> 02:32.670
I didn't bring you along.

02:31.880 --> 02:39.290
The scabs that will never fade

02:34.380 --> 02:36.000
The four of you are incredibly skilled

02:36.000 --> 02:38.670
at working together with your teammates.

02:39.500 --> 02:44.880
That day, a forceful draft snatched it away

02:39.540 --> 02:42.250
I realized that you were the only ones I could count on

02:42.250 --> 02:44.460
to fight without me there.

02:44.880 --> 02:49.500
Unable to change, I have to leave it behind

02:45.250 --> 02:48.000
Go beat your opponent without relying on my strength.

02:48.000 --> 02:49.830
I'm confident you can do it.

02:49.790 --> 02:54.710
Come, outrace your fear

02:51.880 --> 02:53.420
The message ends there.

02:53.420 --> 02:55.040
Damn.

02:54.710 --> 02:58.080
Face the unfamiliar sky and day on your own two feet

02:55.040 --> 02:57.830
For once, there wasn't a single "I just did" in there.

02:57.830 --> 03:00.330
I can tell just how much he wanted to encourage us.

02:58.080 --> 03:00.920
And greet the sunrise

03:00.960 --> 03:02.670
Leave the planning to me.

03:01.380 --> 03:03.960
Misfortune gave rise to happiness

03:03.420 --> 03:06.130
I'm not going to let that woman get away.

03:03.960 --> 03:06.710
You saw a guidepost at the end of despair

03:06.130 --> 03:07.330
You got it.

03:06.710 --> 03:12.040
And now, it's lit with a single flame

03:07.330 --> 03:09.630
Lily and I'll go after Olivia.

03:10.420 --> 03:14.380
If you need, Mr. Johnny can track her scent.

03:12.040 --> 03:14.460
Shake off the entangled past

03:14.380 --> 03:17.710
That's as much as I can really help right now.

03:14.460 --> 03:22.380
And fight until you find a place your heart can soar

03:18.630 --> 03:20.130
You've already done plenty.

03:20.290 --> 03:21.960
If it weren't for your little ones,

03:21.960 --> 03:23.960
we all woulda died back there.

03:22.380 --> 03:28.330
Ah, surviving through each moment

03:26.210 --> 03:28.330
Let's go prove ourselves, shall we?

03:28.330 --> 03:32.290
We're plenty great on our own, even without Teach!

03:33.080 --> 03:38.380
<b>MISSION: Daughter Dearest IV</b>

03:38.000 --> 03:39.750
<i>The moon that night was full,</i>

03:39.750 --> 03:43.380
<i>just like it is tonight.</i>

03:45.540 --> 03:48.460
<i>I was born in a small country to the east.</i>

03:50.750 --> 03:53.130
<i>I spent my days as a prostitute
out in the backcountry,</i>

03:53.460 --> 03:56.290
<i>and I always assumed that my life
would end there just like it began.</i>

04:07.170 --> 04:08.420
You're up.

04:08.420 --> 04:11.710
My gun has a silencer, but even so,

04:11.710 --> 04:14.380
it takes a bold spirit to sleep through
something like this.

04:14.710 --> 04:17.920
Now, I'm going to need you to jump out that window.

04:18.630 --> 04:23.460
You went mad, stole a gun that
one of your johns happened to have,

04:23.460 --> 04:24.670
and went on a killing spree.

04:24.670 --> 04:26.630
Then, you jumped to your death.

04:26.630 --> 04:28.500
That's the plot of this little story.

04:28.750 --> 04:33.290
This is what happens when a politician like him
chases after too many skirts.

04:33.830 --> 04:37.210
But why kill all the others?

04:37.210 --> 04:41.670
If a single politician died,
it would look like the work of an assassin spy.

04:41.670 --> 04:46.920
If a bunch of unrelated people die, though,
they'll write it off as a regular old tragedy.

04:47.210 --> 04:49.330
Now, hurry up and jump.

04:49.630 --> 04:52.920
If you're lucky, you might even survive.

04:53.830 --> 04:57.460
<i>Those eyes of his were so different</i>

04:57.460 --> 04:59.670
<i>than all the uninspired gazes I'd seen before.</i>

05:00.040 --> 05:01.830
<i>It was like he was a prince from another dimension.</i>

05:02.630 --> 05:06.170
<i>They took my frigid body
and gave it warmth once more.</i>

05:09.170 --> 05:11.710
Please, take me away from here.

05:23.500 --> 05:25.130
You've got a knack for this.

05:26.960 --> 05:31.170
<i>Roland was a master assassin feared the world over,</i>

05:31.880 --> 05:34.420
<i>and I became his apprentice.</i>

05:37.460 --> 05:41.290
<i>I had days full of slaughter, jaw-dropping wages,</i>

05:41.290 --> 05:45.670
<i>and sublime affection from the best assassin around.</i>

05:46.290 --> 05:50.580
<i>I could never have gotten any of that out in the sticks!</i>

05:53.330 --> 05:56.460
There's a man you need to watch out for.

05:56.830 --> 06:00.920
I told you that one of our spies took out Inferno, right?

06:01.080 --> 06:04.040
Well, one of its members survived.

06:04.040 --> 06:09.750
At the moment, that man is the most
dangerous individual in the Din Republic.

06:11.960 --> 06:17.170
Bonfire, the Dust King, Ax, Lone, Practical, Crowbar...

06:17.540 --> 06:23.130
He goes by many names,
but the most common one he uses is Klaus.

06:23.130 --> 06:27.380
If you run into him, get in touch with me immediately.

06:27.670 --> 06:28.670
That's a good idea.

06:28.670 --> 06:31.040
No spy from a backwater nation like this
would stand a chance against you.

06:31.040 --> 06:34.250
No, this man's skills are on par with mine.

06:34.250 --> 06:36.460
He could well become my rival.

06:37.080 --> 06:38.380
Your rival?

06:38.380 --> 06:40.290
Even with how talented you are?

06:53.960 --> 06:58.210
Be careful around him, my beloved.

07:04.330 --> 07:06.250
Look at that, you survived.

07:07.210 --> 07:10.290
Pretty sloppy of you not to confirm your kills.

07:10.630 --> 07:11.920
Or what,

07:11.920 --> 07:15.580
was there someone you were so scared of you wanted
to get away as fast as you possibly could?

07:18.580 --> 07:20.790
There's no need for us to get the boss involved.

07:21.210 --> 07:23.040
I'll take you on myself.

07:25.580 --> 07:29.330
Looks like that explosion just now
messed your right arm up pretty bad!

07:35.750 --> 07:38.790
Lotta confidence, comin' from someone
who was so scared of our boss she went running!

07:38.790 --> 07:42.040
Only because Roland acknowledged
Bonfire's strength!

07:42.040 --> 07:43.290
"Roland"?

07:43.290 --> 07:46.380
The man you people were calling Corpse.

07:46.580 --> 07:48.920
I never want to hear that ugly name
out of your mouth again.

07:51.290 --> 07:54.580
Sorry, but if you're lookin' for the gun
you had strapped to your thigh,

07:54.580 --> 07:55.920
I just nicked it.

08:05.790 --> 08:08.170
But my surprise attack was perfect!

08:08.500 --> 08:11.460
Constantly watching out for hostility
is a basic best practice.

08:11.460 --> 08:13.830
Didn't Bonfire teach you that?

08:14.210 --> 08:16.170
This is some impressive poison.

08:16.920 --> 08:19.960
See, this is why I hate prodigies.

08:20.750 --> 08:22.080
Wouldn't you agree, Teach?

08:22.670 --> 08:23.880
You're wide open!

08:26.630 --> 08:29.040
You fuckin' dumbass.

08:30.330 --> 08:32.540
You can have this one back, too!

08:40.000 --> 08:42.630
<i>Why was it those two coming after me
instead of Bonfire?</i>

08:43.380 --> 08:45.670
<i>Was Bonfire never here in the first place?</i>

08:45.960 --> 08:48.830
<i>But then, that man I saw...</i>

08:49.500 --> 08:52.250
<i>must have been the one member of
their team who wasn't there.</i>

08:53.790 --> 08:56.540
I'll put you out of your misery, you crazy bitch.

09:00.540 --> 09:03.380
C'mon, Sybilla, up and at 'em.

09:04.420 --> 09:06.000
I thought I was a goner there.

09:06.000 --> 09:07.380
Take it easy.

09:07.380 --> 09:09.880
That poison puts your body into a
state of suspended animation.

09:09.880 --> 09:12.500
I'm fine 'cuz of my resistance, of course.

09:12.880 --> 09:14.580
Did we manage to trick her?

09:14.580 --> 09:16.540
Yup, everything went right according to plan.

09:16.960 --> 09:19.170
Olivia headed back to the mansion.

09:19.170 --> 09:22.630
Is Grete really gonna be all right?

09:22.630 --> 09:25.130
Fighting ain't exactly her strong suit.

09:25.210 --> 09:28.210
Oh, I don't think there's anything to worry about.

09:28.460 --> 09:31.080
There you go, bein' happy-go-lucky again.

09:31.920 --> 09:34.830
I mean, her resolve's on a whole different level.

09:35.210 --> 09:39.540
So are her plans, her instructions, her leadership,
and the way she props up her heart.

09:40.420 --> 09:45.710
If Olivia makes it back to the mansion,
I'll finish her off myself.

09:46.380 --> 09:48.420
Now, it's her job to complete the mission.

09:49.040 --> 09:52.210
She impersonated Teach himself and
took everything on her back.

09:52.500 --> 09:55.920
There's no way someone with a heart
that strong would ever lose!

09:56.460 --> 09:58.500
All we have to do now is believe in her,

09:58.500 --> 10:00.330
in our strategist.

10:01.540 --> 10:04.290
Go on and do great things, girl.

10:04.290 --> 10:06.210
Win Teach's praise and his love.

10:08.250 --> 10:11.920
<b>MISSION: Daughter Dearest IV</b>

10:23.290 --> 10:24.540
<i>It's okay.</i>

10:24.540 --> 10:26.880
<i>Lily and Sybilla will be fine.</i>

10:27.750 --> 10:29.500
<i>Everything so far is just as I expected.</i>

10:30.290 --> 10:33.880
<i>But I feel like I'm going to be crushed
under the weight of my own fear.</i>

10:34.710 --> 10:37.790
<i>Is this the responsibility the boss has to shoulder?</i>

10:41.710 --> 10:44.290
Would it be all right if I made one request?

10:46.380 --> 10:51.670
Once I complete the mission,
would you hold me in your arms?

10:54.130 --> 10:56.130
It doesn't have to mean anything.

10:56.540 --> 10:59.670
I just want something to help me keep going.

11:03.670 --> 11:04.880
Very well.

11:06.630 --> 11:07.960
It's a promise.

11:08.290 --> 11:11.210
When you come back alive,

11:11.210 --> 11:12.790
I'll hug you as tightly as I can.

11:21.580 --> 11:23.960
I won't run away.

11:27.040 --> 11:29.670
I killed Sybilla and Lily.

11:30.130 --> 11:34.880
If I kill you too, I'll be able to
go back to my job at the mansion.

11:34.880 --> 11:36.080
What?

11:36.080 --> 11:40.080
My job's to take information from Uwe
and pass it along to Roland.

11:40.460 --> 11:43.170
I want to be useful to him.

11:43.750 --> 11:46.170
Now, let's do this.
To the death!

11:57.170 --> 11:58.670
Not good enough by half.

11:58.670 --> 12:01.080
What has Bonfire even been teaching you?

12:01.330 --> 12:03.330
I see no reason to answer that question.

12:03.500 --> 12:06.580
Has he ever made love to you?

12:07.380 --> 12:09.960
Roland's made love to me countless times.

12:10.380 --> 12:13.040
He's showered me with affection,
taught me new skills,

12:13.040 --> 12:16.290
and given me everything I ever wanted.

12:16.290 --> 12:18.250
Oh, how unloved you are.

12:18.250 --> 12:20.000
It's pathetic, really.

12:25.920 --> 12:28.580
That was you in disguise, wasn't it?

12:29.000 --> 12:31.750
That Bonfire I saw?

12:32.540 --> 12:35.380
So, how are planning on using that
talent of yours to take me down?

12:38.880 --> 12:40.250
Jump.

12:40.540 --> 12:42.500
You want me to jump?

12:42.880 --> 12:45.540
You're planning on making it look like I killed myself?

12:45.830 --> 12:49.540
That will let me pin the blame
for Lily and Sybilla's deaths on you.

12:49.790 --> 12:51.710
Now do it, or I shoot.

12:55.420 --> 12:57.000
Lucky you!

12:57.000 --> 13:00.040
Once you're dead, your teacher will finally love you.

13:00.040 --> 13:02.920
Even my death wouldn't be enough for that.

13:04.380 --> 13:07.330
The boss doesn't harbor
any special feelings towards me.

13:07.580 --> 13:09.210
I've known that for a long time.

13:09.210 --> 13:11.380
You really are pathetic, aren't you?

13:11.790 --> 13:13.580
But he made me a promise.

13:14.080 --> 13:16.250
I can't afford to die.

13:16.880 --> 13:21.000
I have to survive if I want the boss
to hold me in his arms.

13:21.460 --> 13:22.920
Well, bad news.

13:22.920 --> 13:25.290
This is the end of the road for you.

13:25.290 --> 13:27.920
Now, hurry up and-

13:36.750 --> 13:38.040
But how?

13:38.880 --> 13:40.880
I didn't sense any hostility.

13:40.880 --> 13:43.830
If I did, I would have been able to dodge the bullet!

13:44.500 --> 13:46.790
Of course you didn't feel any hostility.

13:46.790 --> 13:49.750
That bullet was meant for me.

13:50.210 --> 13:53.580
I know you're up there, killer scum!

13:55.500 --> 13:57.750
Damn it, he escaped again!

13:57.750 --> 14:00.080
It's dangerous out here!
You need to get inside!

14:01.170 --> 14:02.710
Wait, who are you?

14:03.630 --> 14:05.040
What a letdown.

14:05.040 --> 14:07.130
Having the target jump to their death?

14:07.290 --> 14:11.080
I can't believe you took Corpse's signature move
and used it verbatim.

14:11.420 --> 14:14.710
I guess you can only mimic what you were taught.

14:16.130 --> 14:18.330
I'm code name Daughter Dearest.

14:18.670 --> 14:20.960
Now, let's fill this time with laughter and tears.

14:21.460 --> 14:22.710
That birthmark...

14:23.250 --> 14:28.130
The reason I let Uwe see me as the assassin twice

14:28.130 --> 14:30.670
wasn't just to root you out.

14:31.330 --> 14:35.920
It was so he would fire at this birthmarked face
without hesitation.

14:36.330 --> 14:41.330
I'd already made sure that his marksmanship returned
as his night blindness abated.

14:41.580 --> 14:46.080
I knew that his bullet, aimed at the assassin,
would come flying straight at me.

14:46.330 --> 14:50.290
All I had to do was dodge,
and a bullet devoid of hostility

14:50.290 --> 14:52.920
would strike you directly as you stood behind me.

14:53.250 --> 14:54.580
That's impossible.

14:55.040 --> 14:56.290
What part of it?

14:56.790 --> 14:59.130
There's no way you could have
donned a disguise that quickly!

14:59.130 --> 15:01.540
I never gave you a chance to put on a mask!

15:01.960 --> 15:04.290
I didn't put on a disguise.

15:04.460 --> 15:05.670
I did the exact opposite.

15:05.670 --> 15:07.500
I took one off.

15:07.710 --> 15:10.880
Taking off a mask is so easy,
you can do it in an instant.

15:13.290 --> 15:15.130
This is my real face.

15:15.960 --> 15:19.290
This is why nobody ever loved me.

15:22.170 --> 15:23.380
I get it.

15:23.380 --> 15:25.130
It all makes sense now.

15:25.130 --> 15:26.830
So, that's why you're so needy.

15:26.830 --> 15:29.040
No wonder you're so unloved!

15:29.040 --> 15:31.460
See, the thing about women who are loved

15:31.460 --> 15:34.540
is that we don't have to fight ourselves because
we have men who protect us.

15:34.540 --> 15:35.880
A transmitter?!

15:35.880 --> 15:40.670
The moment I saw Bonfire,
I called Roland in to save me.

15:41.130 --> 15:45.000
That turned out to just be you in disguise,
but it all worked out for me in the end.

15:45.000 --> 15:51.000
If you kill me, he'll go mad with rage
and go on a wild rampage.

15:51.000 --> 15:53.540
Because he loves me!

15:53.540 --> 15:54.960
This changes nothing.

15:55.880 --> 15:57.420
It's just as I expected.

15:57.420 --> 15:59.250
Everything is going how I expected.

15:59.250 --> 16:01.170
This time, you're dead!

16:01.330 --> 16:05.040
You can take that hideous, unloved face of yours
with you to the grave!

16:07.710 --> 16:09.420
What a sorry woman you are.

16:09.830 --> 16:11.460
I can't begin to comprehend it.

16:11.880 --> 16:15.880
How can you see her face and not feel anything?

16:16.920 --> 16:18.130
Bonfire!

16:20.210 --> 16:24.290
Even now, I can clearly remember
the sight I saw that day.

16:36.130 --> 16:40.170
The moment I saw her naked face,
I understood everything.

16:40.540 --> 16:45.380
I could tell just how intently she'd built up
her techniques in order to obtain love.

16:45.710 --> 16:48.290
I could tell how much she'd honed herself.

16:48.750 --> 16:53.170
Her face spoke of a radiantly magnificent heart,

16:53.170 --> 16:55.210
and I found myself enchanted by it.

16:56.330 --> 16:58.790
That's why I couldn't help but say,

16:59.420 --> 17:01.380
"How beautiful."

17:05.920 --> 17:07.380
Where's Roland?

17:07.750 --> 17:09.330
Right there in front of you.

17:11.330 --> 17:13.290
Olivia?

17:13.290 --> 17:14.500
But how?!

17:14.500 --> 17:16.420
You said you were evenly matched with him!

17:16.630 --> 17:17.830
Evenly matched?

17:18.500 --> 17:20.040
That reminds me, I had a question.

17:20.040 --> 17:25.080
As soon as I ran into him, he starting babbling
some nonsense about us being rivals.

17:25.880 --> 17:27.250
Do you know what that was about?

17:27.250 --> 17:28.670
What do you mean?

17:28.670 --> 17:30.170
I mean, he was a pushover.

17:30.750 --> 17:33.670
As the World's Strongest, he was no match for me.

17:37.250 --> 17:38.630
He's lying, right?

17:38.630 --> 17:40.330
This isn't really happening, right?

17:40.330 --> 17:42.330
Please, Roland, say something!

17:42.330 --> 17:44.330
Olivia...

17:44.630 --> 17:46.420
Save me...

17:48.250 --> 17:52.630
No, no! Why is this happening?!

17:52.630 --> 17:53.710
Grete...

17:53.710 --> 17:55.790
On it, I came prepared.

17:56.380 --> 17:58.710
You two have taken too many lives.

17:59.420 --> 18:03.880
Shadow war or not, your actions are unacceptable.

18:04.580 --> 18:06.210
I hope you've made your peace.

18:06.500 --> 18:07.830
My peace?

18:07.830 --> 18:10.130
He never taught me about this.

18:10.500 --> 18:11.710
I see.

18:11.710 --> 18:14.380
Now I understand why you lost.

18:19.830 --> 18:23.960
You people aren't qualified to be our enemies.

18:29.460 --> 18:32.920
I've been watching the night as it pours on down

18:32.920 --> 18:35.580
Even as it gets closer and closer

18:35.580 --> 18:37.830
(Give it up, give it up)

18:38.170 --> 18:41.790
If I quietly gave you my secret name

18:41.790 --> 18:47.460
I could vanish into the dark to avoid being found

18:55.000 --> 18:58.670
I've forgotten all about those secret tears I shed

18:58.670 --> 19:02.170
Like my cells all got replaced

19:02.170 --> 19:04.540
I'm a different person now

19:04.880 --> 19:08.290
So let's frolic our way through these busy days

19:08.290 --> 19:11.080
I kind of want to talk to you

19:11.080 --> 19:13.330
But everyone is gone

19:13.330 --> 19:17.080
That's not what it means

19:17.080 --> 19:20.540
To make someone a promise

19:22.580 --> 19:26.130
I've been watching the night as it pours on down

19:26.130 --> 19:28.960
Even as it gets closer and closer

19:28.960 --> 19:31.210
(Give it up, give it up)

19:31.500 --> 19:35.130
If I quietly gave you my secret name

19:35.130 --> 19:40.290
I could vanish into the dark to avoid being found

19:40.290 --> 19:41.750
And when we're born again

19:41.750 --> 19:44.080
Flying through a new night sky

19:44.080 --> 19:48.710
We intersect again and again

19:48.880 --> 19:50.380
Standing on level stars

19:50.380 --> 19:52.920
And gazing straight into each other's eyes

19:52.920 --> 19:57.630
I want to give it to you when we meet again

20:00.500 --> 20:04.750
The mission's finally over,
so let's end it by going for a drive together.

20:05.080 --> 20:07.830
I do believe it was Lily who made that suggestion.

20:08.130 --> 20:09.330
It was.

20:10.790 --> 20:12.960
That girl lies as easily as she breathes.

20:15.290 --> 20:18.380
Thanks to my bold scheme,

20:18.380 --> 20:22.630
Grete's probably sobbing with gratitude
right about now!

20:23.080 --> 20:24.670
Do you think she's actually crying?

20:24.670 --> 20:26.000
Hell if I know.

20:27.130 --> 20:30.580
Still, she worked her ass off this time around.

20:31.460 --> 20:33.040
I'd say she's earned this much.

20:45.170 --> 20:49.710
Grete, I've done a lot of thinking over this past month.

20:50.290 --> 20:57.670
I was trying to figure out what the best way for me
to respond to your love would be,

20:57.670 --> 21:00.830
both as your boss, as the Greatest Spy
in the World, and as a man.

21:02.420 --> 21:04.170
Were you able to reach a conclusion?

21:05.500 --> 21:06.710
I was.

21:16.580 --> 21:19.750
I decided to ignore all my ideals,
responsibilities, and pretenses

21:19.750 --> 21:22.460
and tell you how I truly felt as a man.

21:25.420 --> 21:29.460
Grete, I hold no romantic attraction towards you.

21:30.500 --> 21:32.290
I can't return your feelings.

21:33.830 --> 21:34.830
I see.

21:35.750 --> 21:38.380
However, I don't want you to misunderstand me.

21:39.290 --> 21:43.830
I've never felt romantic attraction towards anyone.

21:45.580 --> 21:48.250
Romantic love isn't what I'm looking for.

21:48.710 --> 21:50.920
What I want is familial love.

21:52.330 --> 21:56.960
The kind of bonds that form over the course of both
harsh missions and peaceful downtimes.

21:58.750 --> 22:03.040
That's why I can't return your romantic love.

22:03.670 --> 22:05.790
I can't love you as a woman,

22:05.790 --> 22:08.750
and if you end up developing feelings
for some other man,

22:08.750 --> 22:10.880
then I'll have no right to get in your way.

22:12.790 --> 22:16.540
But if you're willing to stay by my side,

22:17.210 --> 22:20.580
then I would like very much to love you
as a member of my family.

22:23.580 --> 22:25.500
I have a request.

22:54.420 --> 22:56.790
Could you say something?

22:57.880 --> 23:01.750
Please, tell me how you see me.

23:02.670 --> 23:05.290
There's only one thing I possibly could say.

23:10.330 --> 23:13.790
Grete, you're beautiful.
